### 1. Create student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Jane Smith", "email": "jane@example.com" }

### 1b. Invalid create — field errors
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "", "email": "not-an-email" }

### 1c. Duplicate email — 409
# Run request 1 first.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Another Jane", "email": "jane@example.com" }

### 2. Get student by id — note the ETag response header
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1

### 2b. PUT without If-Match — 428
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane@example.com", "phoneNumber": null, "status": "ACTIVE" }

### 2c. PUT with a stale If-Match — 412
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "99"

{ "fullName": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane@example.com", "phoneNumber": null, "status": "ACTIVE" }

### 2d. PUT with the correct If-Match — succeeds, ETag becomes "1"
# Read the ETag from request 2's response before running this.
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{ "fullName": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane@example.com", "phoneNumber": "+15550001111", "status": "ACTIVE" }

### 3. PATCH — merge-patch sets only the mentioned field
# Use whatever ETag GET /students/1 currently returns.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
If-Match: "1"

{ "phoneNumber": "+15559998888" }

### 3b. PATCH with explicit null — clears phoneNumber
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
If-Match: "2"

{ "phoneNumber": null }

### 3c. PATCH with explicit null on a required field — 400
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
If-Match: "3"

{ "fullName": null }

### 3d. PATCH with the wrong Content-Type — 415
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "3"

{ "phoneNumber": "+15550001111" }

### 4. List students — pagination + sort
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students?page=0&size=20&sortBy=fullName&sortDir=asc

### 4b. Unknown sort field — clean 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students?sortBy=bogus

### 5. Delete student
# Create a throwaway student first if you want to see this succeed without breaking the flow below.
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1

### 6. Create a course (starts DRAFT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Intro to REST", "description": "Basics of resource design", "capacity": 10 }

### 6b. Publish the course
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1/publish

### 6c. Publish again — 409, already PUBLISHED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1/publish

### 6d. Archive the course
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1/archive

### 7. PATCH course — clear description with explicit null
# Use a fresh DRAFT course id and its current ETag.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
If-Match: "0"

{ "description": null }

### 8. Create a fresh student and a small-capacity course for the enrollment flow
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Bob Jones", "email": "bob@example.com" }

### 8b.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Small Course", "description": "capacity 1", "capacity": 1 }

### 9. Enroll before the course is published — 409
# Use the ids created in 8/8b.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 2, "courseId": 2 }

### 9b. Publish it
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/2/publish

### 10. Enroll — succeeds
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 2, "courseId": 2 }

### 10b. Enroll the same student again — 409, duplicate active enrollment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 2, "courseId": 2 }

### 10c. Enroll a second student — 409, course at capacity (capacity was 1)
# Create a third student first, then try enrolling them here.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 3, "courseId": 2 }

### 11. Relationship views
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/2/students

### 11b.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/2/courses

### 12. Complete the enrollment
# Use the enrollment id returned by request 10.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments/1/complete

### 12b. Complete it again — 409, no longer ACTIVE
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/enrollments/1/complete

### 13. Delete the course while it still has an active enrollment — 409
# Try this before completing/dropping the enrollment above.
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/2

### 14. Versioning — v1 keeps fullName whole, v2 splits it
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/2

### 14b.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v2/students/2
